---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Note from '../components/Note.astro';
import { url } from '../utils';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Greg Hansell, an Australian artist working in pastel from his studio in the Hawkesbury region of New South Wales."
>
  <div class="container section">
    <article class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Greg Hansell</h1>

      <Note kind="check">
        This biography was drafted from public sources (gallery, museum and council websites).
        Check every detail against Greg's book before relying on it.
      </Note>

      <Note>Add a portrait photo of Greg here.</Note>

      <p class="lede">
        Greg Hansell is an Australian artist who works in pastel.
      </p>
      <p>
        Born in Goulburn, New South Wales, in 1949, Greg studied art at St George Technical College
        in the late 1970s and has painted full time since 1980. He lives and works near Windsor in
        the Hawkesbury region of NSW, where his house, studio and garden often find their way into
        his pictures.
      </p>

      <h2>The work</h2>
      <p>
        Much of Greg's work looks closely at weathered, man-made surfaces: corrugated iron, timber,
        old farm implements and machinery, and the way Australian light falls across them. He is
        known for his earth pastels, which he makes by hand from rocks and clays.
      </p>
      <Note>Add an artist statement in Greg's own words.</Note>

      <h2>Recognition</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Hung in the Wynne Prize at the Art Gallery of New South Wales many times.</li>
        <li>Twice winner of the Mosman Art Prize.</li>
        <li>Exhibitions with the Historic Houses Trust of NSW, now Museums of History NSW.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href={url('/exhibitions/')}>Exhibitions and prizes →</a></p>

      <h2>Collections</h2>
      <p>
        Greg's work is held in public and corporate collections, including the Historic Houses
        Trust of NSW, Hawkesbury City Council, Camden Council, the Commonwealth Bank and ANZ.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
